15 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Comparison graphic displaying leaves from two cannabis genotypes "Kanada" and "Terra Italia", showing distinct differences in leaf size and shape. Leaves of the genotype "Terra Italia" are larger and broader, with a 10 cm scale for reference.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Two cannabis flower clusters are shown side by side against a black background, labeled Kanada on the left and Terra Italia on the right, each accompanied by a labeled plant marker and a ruler for size comparison.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating drought stress events and sampling points in an experiment with three treatments: control, moderate stress, and severe stress, across four harvest times labeled as 15, 46, 60, and 79 days after planting. Yellow stars represent sampling points, blue lines represent treatment duration, and green and red segments indicate periods of moderate and severe stress, respectively, with arrows indicating progression.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Composite image displaying two groups of three cannabis plants each against a black background. The top row, labeled \215KANADA \(KAN\)\216, shows control, moderate stress, and severe stress conditions with a 50-centimeter scale. The bottom row, labeled \215TERRA ITALIA \(TIT\)\216, shows the same stress levels with a 70-centimeter scale. Major leaves are indicated by arrows in both moderate and severe stress plants. Plants under increased stress appear smaller, with fewer and more wilted leaves.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Grouped scatter plot with fitted curves showing container capacity percentage over time for genotypes KAN and TIT under control, moderate, and severe drought stress, separated by early, mid, and late drought events, illustrating lower container capacity with increasing drought severity and consistent genotype trends across events.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Two scatter plots compare the relationship between CC percentage and E \(mmol per square meter per second\) for two cannabis genotypes: Kanada on the left and Terra Italia on the right. Each plot includes black data points, a negative trend line, and a shaded confidence interval, indicating E decreases as CC percentage declines.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Two-panel scientific figure displaying scatter plots with regression lines and shaded confidence intervals for two genotypes, KANADA and TERRA ITALIA, under PAR of two thousand. Panel A shows photosynthetic rate \(A, in micromoles per square meter per second\) versus container capacity \(CC percent\), while panel B shows stomatal conductance \(millimoles per square meter per second\) versus CC percent. Both traits decrease as CC percent decreases for both genotypes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot with trend lines displaying the relationship between container capacity \(CC, x-axis\) and water use efficiency index \(WUEi, y-axis\) for two genotypes: KANADA and TERRA ITALIA. Data are categorized by treatment: control \(black\), moderate continuous \(red\), severe early \(blue\), severe middle \(green\), and severe late \(purple\). Points show higher WUEi with decreasing CC. Red trend lines with shaded confidence intervals represent moderate continuous treatment in both regions.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Grouped bar chart comparing leaf area across two genotypes, KAN and TIT, at four stages \(DAP 15, 46, 60, 79\), with five treatments: control, moderate continuous, severe-early, severe-mid, and severe-late. KAN shows similar leaf area for all treatments at each stage, labeled \215ns\216 for not significant. TIT shows significant decreases at DAP seventy-nine, with severe-mid and severe-late having notably lower leaf areas, labeled \215b\216 and \215c.\216 Error bars indicate variability. Legend identifies treatments by color.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
